    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d599">

                <pb facs="0893" n="879" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg879"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/10–2848</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Executive Secretary of the National Security Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Souers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-28">October 28,
                        1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Admiral Souers</hi>: You will recall that it is
                    provided in NSC 13/2, “Recommendations With
                    Respect to U.S. Policy Toward Japan”, approved by the President on October 9,
                    that recommendations on the subject of the Far Eastern Commission are to be
                    submitted separately. Omission of the section on this subject from NSC 13/2 was necessitated by the inability of the
                    State and Army Departments to reach complete agreement on certain language in
                    the pertinent section in NSC 13/1.</p>
                <p>I am now able to inform you that the enclosed draft paragraph on this subject
                    proposed by the Department of the Army has been accepted by the Department of
                    State. It is accordingly requested that <pb facs="0894" n="880" xml:id="pg880"/>
                    appropriate steps be taken to secure the Council’s approval for the paragraph
                    and to incorporate it in NSC 13/2.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert A. Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d599-a1.xml" xpointer="d599-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
